</div>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The time between timer events can be longer than that specified with <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlSetTimerEvent" target="_blank">llSetTimerEvent</a>, this is caused by:
    <ul>
      <li><b>Time dilation</b> - See <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlGetRegionTimeDilation" target="_blank">llGetRegionTimeDilation</a> for more information;</li>
      <li><b>Default event delay</b> - Only so many events can be triggered per second;</li>
      <li><b>Event Execution</b> - If the execution of an event takes too long;</li>
      <li><b>llSleep()</b>.</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
    <li>Only one timer can be active at one time.</li>
    <li>The timer survives state changes, but does not survive resets.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

local gap = 2.0
local counter = 0.0

local function main()
    -- Activate the timer listener every 2 seconds
    ll.SetTimerEvent(gap)
end

function LLEvents.timer()
    counter = counter + gap
    ll.Say(0, tostring(counter) .. " seconds have passed")
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`float gap = 2.0;
float counter = 0.0;

default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        // Activate the timer listener every 2 seconds
        llSetTimerEvent(gap);
    }

    timer()
    {
        counter = counter + gap; 
        llSay(0, (string)counter+" seconds have passed");
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
